ribute to the 401 k plan  to $2,400 now a relevant question is  well cutting it to $2,400 from what and  that is the next thing we have to talk  about in 2017 the contribution limit for  401ks is $18,000  next year the contribution limit for  401k is is scheduled to go up to  eighteen thousand five hundred dollars  so this is a major cut and it is Bigley  regressive and regressive not in the  you're part of the regressive left sense  regressive in the tax sense right it  will impact the middle class way more  than it will impact the rich and that  happens in a number of ways if you make  fifty thousand dollars the tax savings  provided by the deductibility of 401k  contributions really makes a difference  to you if you make 50k and you put five  thousand dollars in a 401k that saves  you one thousand two hundred and fifty  dollars in taxes because you're at the  twenty five percent federal tax rate  that's about a hundred dollars a month a  hundred dollars a month is real money  for someone that's grossing fifty  thousand dollars if you live in  Massachusetts you're saving another 5.3  percent on your state income tax that's  another two hundred and sixty-five  dollars so we're talking about fifteen  hundred dollars a year in your pocket if  you earn fifty thousand dollars live in  Massachusetts and contribute five grand  to your 401k compare that to someone  earning four hundred thousand dollars a  year if you earn four hundred thousand  dollars a year and you contribute the  full eighteen thousand dollars that  you're allowed even at the thirty five  percent tax bracket that you'd be in  that eighteen thousand dollars saves you  sixty three hundred in taxes if you're  earning thirty three thousand dollars a  month the way you would be if you earned  four hundred thousand dollars a year  what is five hundred bucks a month do  for you you're not making big decisions  about lifestyle based on those five  hundred bucks  you're probably saving a lot of that  money so i